{%- comment -%}
  Zero-pads a 1-based position to the two-digit form the About board draws:
  1 -> 01, 9 -> 09, 10 -> 10.

  Accepts:
    position - required, the 1-based index. Pass `forloop.index`.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'bf-about-number', position: forloop.index -%}

  A snippet rather than a filter chain because `prepend: '0'` is wrong the moment
  a run reaches ten rows, and rather than an `assign` because `render` runs in an
  isolated scope — a variable set in here is not visible to the caller. This one
  OUTPUTS, so it is called where the digits belong.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if position < 10 -%}0{%- endif -%}
{{- position -}}
